foreign  Battleground Paris  for hours police and protesters charged  against each other in the French capital  Kurdish demonstrators are angry at  Authority's response to the attack on  Friday which killed three refugees  they want answers from the police why  did it take so long for them to respond  to the attack why have they not  designated this a terrorist attack and  why wasn't security provided to the  cultural center after it had earlier  been asked for  we've been working on the 10th  anniversary of the killing of our three  comrades ten years later we the Kurdish  women are still asking for justice and  now again our blood is spilled in France  we are angry and the French state is  responsible  they refused to remain confined to one  square where the police allowed them to  protest Kurdish demonstrators say the  bullets fired in the attack were felt by  every member of their community  as the protests have calmed down here in  Paris the police and security services  are out in force clearing the protesters  from the street going from Republic  Square to Bastille square but the anger  in the streets of Paris continues  as more videos emerge from Witnesses  some show onlookers overpowering the  attacker security sources say he still  had multiple magazines and dozens of  rounds of ammunition  Eunice witnessed the attacker targeting  the cultural center a restaurant and the  nababu's shop he says the 69 year old  man knew where he wanted to open fire  the state want us to believe it's a  resist attack but the guy was released  from detention 10 days ago in 10 days he  found guns and came here we want to know  we want the state to answer  the killings have touched a nerve among  France's migrant communities with  protests in other cities as well they  want to know why an attack on a minority  Community isn't being designated a  terrorist attack  these kids chanted and called for  revenge and unless the government can  satisfy their demands their anger is  unlikely to go away  from Paris

